{# The npm lockfile Dockerfile.browser installs from, shipped verbatim.

   A template with nothing in it but one interpolation, on purpose: that is what
   puts the file through the same path every other generated file takes -- the
   render loop, `stencil gen --dry-run`, `stencil clean`, and the managed
   .gitignore section, all of which are driven by the template list rather than
   by a second list of files copied some other way.

   The content is stencil/assets/browser-package-lock.json, written by
   scripts/vendor_npm_locks.py. pipeline.read_lockfile() strips its trailing
   newline and the newline at the end of this file puts it back, so the
   generated file is byte-identical to the committed one. #}
